{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,14]],"date-time":"2026-05-14T19:41:38Z","timestamp":1778787698413,"version":"3.51.4"},"reference-count":61,"publisher":"Wiley","issue":"11","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2020,4,24]],"date-time":"2020-04-24T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1587686400000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/termsAndConditions#vor"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100001809","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["21875112"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["21875112"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100001809","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100001809","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["51806224"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["51806224"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100001809","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100012216","name":"Jiangsu University of Science and Technology","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["1062931903"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["1062931903"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100012216","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100012246","name":"Priority Academic Program Development of Jiangsu Higher Education Institutions","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100012246","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":["chemistry-europe.onlinelibrary.wiley.com"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["ChemCatChem"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2020,6,5]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title><jats:p>Hydrogen energy is considered as an ideal candidate energy of traditional fossil fuels. Oxygen evolution reaction (OER) is a crucial reaction for the sustainable hydrogen generation as a half reaction of water splitting. It is important to develop efficient electrocatalysts for the OER. Herein, the porous iridium nanowires (Ir PNWs) with polyallylamine hydrochloride (PAH) as a complex\u2010forming agent and capping agent have been successfully synthesized through a one\u2010pot hydrothermal approach. Benefiting from the inherent anisotropic characteristic of one\u2010dimensional nanowires structure, abundant microporous channels and high atom utilization efficiency, the synthesized Ir PNWs possess very large electrochemically active surface area (118.2\u2005m<jats:sup>2<\/jats:sup>\u2009g<jats:sup>\u22121<\/jats:sup>), and thus exhibit superior electrocatalytic activity and stability towards the OER compared with commercial RuO<jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub> catalyst and other Ir nanocrystals.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/cctc.202000388","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2020,3,24]],"date-time":"2020-03-24T05:38:46Z","timestamp":1585028326000},"page":"3060-3067","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":33,"title":["Ultrafine Ir Nanowires with Microporous Channels and Superior Electrocatalytic Activity for Oxygen Evolution Reaction"],"prefix":"10.1002","volume":"12","author":[{"given":"Zhenyuan","family":"Liu","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Materials Science and Engineering Jiangsu University of Science and Technology  Zhenjiang Jiangsu 212003 P.R. China"},{"name":"Jiangsu Key Laboratory of New Power Batteries Jiangsu Collaborative Innovation Centre of Biomedical Functional Materials School of Chemistry and Materials Science Nanjing Normal University  Nanjing Jiangsu 210023 P.R. China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Jiahui","family":"Li","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Jiangsu Key Laboratory of New Power Batteries Jiangsu Collaborative Innovation Centre of Biomedical Functional Materials School of Chemistry and Materials Science Nanjing Normal University  Nanjing Jiangsu 2